#11603
"South End of a Long Hall"
"The southern end of long hall, with a huge feast table lying in its center,
surrounded by many chairs.  This table appears to have seen much use, and is
scarred and pitted.  The walls and floor in this room echo the theme of this
place, the walls being of a creamy shade of marble, and the floor of dark
obsidian colored stone.  The walls are set with sconces, set an equal distance
apart, and there are candelabra on the table, which serve to provide light for
the large room.  A door on the east wall is carved with a mask motif.
"
""
