#11604
"North End of a Long Hall"
"The northern end of a long feast hall, with a feast table as a centrepiece.
The dcor here continues in the same vein as the southern end of the hall, with
cream walls and obsidian floor.  A larger chair is set at this end of the
table, possibly where a senior member might sit to preside over meals.  The
hall continues to the east, while to the west is the distinct smell of soup.
"
